// The rogue automatons' pack tactic (was the hard-coded `RaiderBrain`). Distances are shares of the weapon
// reach, so it works for any armed ship: a raider (cannon, 75 m) engages from 90 m, attacks from 64 m and
// orbits at 50 m. It fits the two rule slots of one automaton core. PLACEHOLDER numbers.
// Retuned on 12 Oct 2026 for the faster ships (GDR-0042): at 50 m / 45 m the pack sat inside the Halvex
// Runner's pulse lasers (60 m) and beams (45 m) and died within a second or two each; now it shoots from just
// outside the pulse lasers and circles just outside the beams (see docs/sim.md "Behaviors").
(
    id: "raider_basic",
    name: "Raider pack",
    summary: "Close in and shoot, then strafe around the target for a few seconds, and again.",
    description: "Picks the nearest enemy. Within engagement range it attacks for five seconds out of every nine and circles the target for the other four, so a pack never sits still in front of the guns.",
    tags: ["automaton", "attack"],
    target: "nearest",
    rules: [
        "when target_in_range(120%) and cycle(9s) >= 5s -> orbit(67%)",
        "always -> approach(85%)",
    ],
)
